hub='''<section class="blog-section site-shell"><div class="blog-intro"><h2>Practical answers from a Tampa Bay cleaning company</h2><p>Use these guides to compare cleaning types, prepare for a move, maintain floors and understand professional cleaning. Service pages remain the place to check availability, pricing and booking.</p></div><div class="blog-grid"><article class="blog-card featured"><span>Move-Out Cleaning</span><h2><a href="/blog/move-out-cleaning-to-get-your-deposit-back/">Move-Out Cleaning and Your Security Deposit: A Tampa Bay Renter's Guide</a></h2><p>What cleaning can help with, what it cannot guarantee, and how to prepare for a final walkthrough.</p></article><article class="blog-card"><span>Floor Care</span><h2><a href="/blog/how-to-mop-floors-without-streaks-best-practices-for-5-common-flooring-types/">How to Mop Floors Without Streaks</a></h2><p>Technique and product guidance for five common flooring types.</p></article><article class="blog-card"><span>Apartment Cleaning</span><h2><a href="/blog/apartment-cleaning-services-in-tampa-bay-deep-cleaning-move-out-cleaning--more-for-a-spotless-hom/">Apartment Cleaning: Standard, Deep or Move-Out?</a></h2><p>Choose the cleaning level that matches routine upkeep, a reset or final move.</p></article></div><aside class="blog-cta"><div><h2>Looking for a cleaning service?</h2><p>Compare Tampa Bay Shine services or check eligible residential pricing online.</p></div><div><a class="blog-btn" href="/services/">View Services</a><a class="blog-btn secondary" href="/booknow">Get Pricing</a></div></aside></section>'''
move='''<article class="blog-article site-shell"><div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer</strong><p>Professional move-out cleaning can help you return a rental in cleaner condition, but no cleaning company can guarantee a security-deposit refund. Deposit decisions can also involve damage, lease terms, unpaid charges and other factors outside cleaning.</p></div><h2>Start with your lease and move-out instructions</h2><p>Review the lease, resident portal and any written checklist from the landlord or property manager. Those instructions should control your final preparation. Pay attention to appliance interiors, cabinets, bathrooms, floors, trash removal, keys and the condition expected at the walkthrough.</p><h2>What a move-out clean should focus on</h2><p>For an empty or substantially empty property, high-value work includes kitchen surfaces, appliance interiors when included, empty cabinet and drawer interiors, bathroom buildup, baseboards, closet shelving and final floors.</p><div class="blog-callout"><h3>Cleaning versus damage</h3><p>Cleaning addresses soil, dust, grease, residue and ordinary buildup. It does not repair holes, broken fixtures, permanent stains or damaged flooring. Photograph the property after belongings are removed and again after cleaning.</p></div><h2>A practical final-walkthrough sequence</h2><ol><li>Remove belongings and trash before detailed cleaning.</li><li>Keep electricity and water on through cleaning and inspection.</li><li>Empty appliances, cabinets, drawers and closets that need interior cleaning.</li><li>Provide parking, gate, elevator or lockbox instructions.</li><li>Walk the property in good light and photograph each room.</li><li>Complete landlord-specific tasks outside the cleaning scope.</li></ol><h2>When to book</h2><p>Schedule after movers are finished whenever possible, while leaving time before key return to address anything found during the final walkthrough.</p><div class="related-guides"><h2>Plan your move-out</h2><p><a href="/move-out-cleaning-checklist/">Room-by-room checklist</a> &middot; <a href="/move-out-cleaning-cost-time-guide-tampa-bay/">Cost and timing guide</a> &middot; <a href="/move-out-cleaning-tampa-1/">Move-out service areas</a></p></div><div class="blog-cta"><div><h2>Prefer professional move-out cleaning?</h2><p>Review Tampa Bay Shine's move-in and move-out cleaning options.</p></div><div><a class="blog-btn" href="/move-out-cleaning-tampa-1/">Move-Out Service</a><a class="blog-btn secondary" href="/booknow">Check Pricing</a></div></div></article>'''
mop='''<article class="blog-article site-shell"><div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer</strong><p>Streak-free mopping depends on correct cleaner concentration, a clean mop pad, minimal water and frequent rinse or pad changes. Always follow the flooring manufacturer's care instructions first.</p></div><h2>Why floors look streaky after mopping</h2><p>Common causes include too much cleaner, dirty mop water, repeatedly spreading dissolved soil, residue-forming products or excessive moisture.</p><h2>Technique that works across many hard floors</h2><ol><li>Vacuum or dry-mop loose grit first.</li><li>Dilute cleaner exactly as directed.</li><li>Use a clean microfiber pad or mop head.</li><li>Work in manageable sections without flooding the surface.</li><li>Change dirty water or pads before redistributing soil.</li><li>Allow the floor to dry before heavy foot traffic.</li></ol><div class="floor-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Floor</th><th>Primary concern</th><th>Approach</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ceramic/porcelain tile</td><td>Residue</td><td>Compatible neutral cleaner and clean solution.</td></tr><tr><td>Luxury vinyl</td><td>Film/excess moisture</td><td>Manufacturer-approved product and damp mop.</td></tr><tr><td>Laminate</td><td>Moisture at seams</td><td>Very little liquid; no standing water.</td></tr><tr><td>Sealed hardwood</td><td>Finish/moisture</td><td>Product approved for the specific finish.</td></tr><tr><td>Natural stone</td><td>Etching</td><td>Stone-safe, pH-appropriate cleaner.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Should you mop with vinegar?</h2><p>Vinegar is acidic and is not a universal floor cleaner. It can be inappropriate for natural stone and may conflict with care instructions for other finishes. Check the flooring or finish manufacturer's guidance.</p><h2>When repeated mopping does not fix the appearance</h2><p>Persistent haze may indicate accumulated residue, finish wear, grout soil or a floor-care problem ordinary maintenance mopping will not solve.</p><div class="blog-cta"><div><h2>Need professional floor care?</h2><p>Review floor-cleaning options for homes and commercial properties.</p></div><div><a class="blog-btn" href="/floor-cleaning/">Floor Cleaning</a><a class="blog-btn secondary" href="/contact-us/">Request a Quote</a></div></div></article>'''
apt='''<article class="blog-article site-shell"><div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer</strong><p>Choose standard cleaning for routine upkeep, deep cleaning for an occupied apartment that needs a detailed reset, and move-in/move-out cleaning for an empty or substantially empty apartment where vacancy-related details become accessible.</p></div><h2>Standard cleaning: ongoing maintenance</h2><p>Standard cleaning fits an occupied, generally maintained apartment. The goal is recurring upkeep of kitchens, bathrooms, dusting and floors.</p><h2>Deep cleaning: an occupied-home reset</h2><p>Deep cleaning makes sense for a first professional visit, accumulated buildup or a home needing additional detail before recurring maintenance.</p><h2>Move-out cleaning: prepare the empty apartment for handoff</h2><p>Once belongings are removed, cleaners can address areas difficult to reach during normal maintenance. Depending on scope, that can include appliance interiors, empty cabinets and drawers, closet shelving, baseboards, bathrooms and final floors.</p><div class="floor-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Best starting point</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Routine occupied apartment</td><td>Standard</td><td>Maintenance-focused</td></tr><tr><td>Occupied apartment with buildup</td><td>Deep</td><td>Detailed reset</td></tr><tr><td>Empty apartment before key return</td><td>Move-Out</td><td>Vacancy-related detail</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>What leasing offices may care about</h2><p>Requirements vary by property. Follow your lease and the leasing office's written instructions. Cleaning can improve presentation and remove ordinary soil, but it does not repair damage or override lease obligations.</p><div class="related-guides"><h2>Related resources</h2><p><a href="/apartment-cleaning-services/">Apartment cleaning services</a> &middot; <a href="/apartment-move-out-cleaning/">Apartment move-out cleaning</a> &middot; <a href="/move-out-cleaning-checklist/">Move-out checklist</a></p></div><div class="blog-cta"><div><h2>Choose your apartment cleaning service</h2><p>Compare residential cleaning options and eligible pricing online.</p></div><div><a class="blog-btn" href="/apartment-cleaning-services/">Apartment Cleaning</a><a class="blog-btn secondary" href="/booknow">Check Pricing</a></div></div></article>'''
